{"term":"窑姐","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"yáojiě","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"prostitute (archaic)","concept":"sex_worker","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"archaic","crude":55,"technical":8,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":72,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'kiln sister'; an archaic Mandarin slang term for a prostitute, historically associated with brothels housed in cave-like or kiln-like structures in northern China.","english_term":"prostitute","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"窑 (kiln / cave dwelling, especially the yaodong cave houses of the Loess Plateau) + 姐 (older sister / woman); documents a historical period when such dwellings housed illicit establishments; mainly encountered in historical fiction, period dramas, and older literature today."}
