{"term":"找小姐","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"zhǎo xiǎojiě","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"soliciting sex","concept":"soliciting","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":22,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":89,"recognition_pct_peak":89,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to look for a Miss/young lady'; a widespread euphemism for seeking out a female sex worker, exploiting the dual meaning of 小姐 as both a polite honorific and sex-worker slang.","english_term":"to solicit a prostitute","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"找 (to look for) + 小姐 (Miss / young lady); in mainland China from the 1990s onward, 小姐 became so strongly associated with sex workers in service-industry contexts that many professional women actively avoid the title — a semantic shift with real social consequences; the phrase is low-crude precisely because its euphemistic cover remains largely intact."}
